<title>USA: Avitar extends warrant expiration date.</title>
<headline>Avitar extends warrant expiration date.</headline>
<dateline>CANTON, Mass. 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Avitar Inc said on Monday it extended the expiration date of its redeemable warrants to April 30 from February 28, and reduced the exercise price so that each warrant can be converted into four shares at $0.85 per share.</p>
<p>Avitar said it has about 2.7 million redeemable warrants outstanding, which potentially could be converted into 11 million common shares at a total price of $9.3 million.</p>
<p>The funds would be used for working capital and for expansion, the company said.</p>
